# Before running: pick the `local` environment in the "Run with" selector at the top of the editor,
# and run `npm run http:tokens` once. Without an environment, variables like api and token stay unresolved.
#
# Internal management port (ADR-016): no auth here, and NOT exposed on the public port.

### 1. Liveness: the process is up (never checks dependencies)
GET {{management}}/health/live

> {%
    client.test("200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status));
%}

### 2. Readiness: Postgres + Kafka consumer reachable (503 when either is down)
GET {{management}}/health/ready

### 3. Prometheus metrics (capacity_*, http_*, kafka lag, Node runtime)
GET {{management}}/metrics

### 4. OpenAPI spec (Swagger UI is at {{management}}/docs in a browser)
GET {{management}}/docs/openapi.json

> {%
    client.test("OpenAPI 3", () => client.assert(response.body.openapi.startsWith("3."), response.body.openapi));
%}

### 5. Health is not on the public port → 404 (no route matches, so the JWT guard never runs)
GET {{apiHost}}/health/live

> {%
    client.test("not on the public port", () => client.assert(response.status === 401 || response.status === 404,
        "status " + response.status));
%}
